      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Manage Claw MCP server ownership",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- apply portable stdio and remote MCP declarations through OpenClaw's validated source-config writer\r\n- preserve `${ENV_VAR}` references and credential-free OAuth intent without storing server configuration in provenance\r\n- classify each declaration with the shared Claw ownership model: `relationship` (`managed` or `referenced`), `origin` (`claw-introduced` or `pre-existing`), and current `independentOwner` evidence\r\n- expose MCP ownership and drift in status/export, reconcile uncertain writes, and support the same explicit referenced-cleanup choices as skills and plugins\r\n\r\n## Contract\r\n\r\n- dry-run shows each MCP command or URL before consent; apply rechecks source config and uses create-only writes\r\n- a collision-free declaration created for the first Claw is managed; an exact pre-existing declaration, or reuse by another Claw, is referenced\r\n- conflicting existing names block add; exact declarations are reused without mutation\r\n- ordinary MCP configuration writes mark current independent ownership; Claw writes do not claim an independent owner\r\n- provenance stores only agent, name, config digest, relationship, origin, current independent-owner evidence, and lifecycle status\r\n- pending writes reconcile deterministically against source-preserving config for both landed and non-landed outcomes\r\n- remove deletes unchanged managed declarations by default; referenced declarations are retained unless the integrity-bound plan selects `remove-if-unused` or an explicit `mcp:<name>` cleanup, with conflict override required when another owner remains\r\n- compare-before-unset prevents removing a declaration that changed after planning; unreadable source config fails closed\r\n- ordinary OpenClaw MCP and agent lifecycles remain authoritative and unchanged\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n- generated Kysely schema verification: passed\r\n- Kysely raw-SQL guardrails: passed\r\n- scoped Oxfmt, Oxlint, and `git diff --check`: passed\r\n- 126 focused schema, MCP, config, lifecycle, export, CLI, and ordinary agent-delete tests passed at pre-documentation head `c5d416c95c0`; current head `c8f2ca2eabd` adds only this stage's documentation after restacking\r\n- live MCP process startup was not exercised; this PR mutates and verifies source configuration only\r\n\r\n```text\r\nTest Files  7 passed (7)\r\nTests       126 passed (126)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Stack\r\n\r\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\r\n- Depends on: #102383 Gateway cron ownership\r\n- This PR: validated MCP source config, common ownership semantics, reconciliation, export, and safe removal\r\n- Next: #102427 projects the complete lifecycle state into doctor diagnostics\r\n\r\nMCP remains a separate stage because OpenClaw config, rather than the agent entry or Gateway scheduler, owns these declarations. The experimental CLI remains gated by `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`.\r\n\r\n## Documentation\r\n\r\nExtends `/cli/claws` with MCP declarations, source-preserving environment references, ownership classification, and lifecycle behavior.\r\n",
